WEBVTT

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:03.690
<b>Death</b>

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:04.910
Death: a convulsion.

00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:09.330
Murder: an idol of the powerless.

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:12.910
I am the angel of murder.

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:14.900
The king of crime.

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:17.410
Rest in peace!

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:02.570
Listen.

00:02:02.570 --> 00:02:05.000
I'll get you out of here.

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:13.560
Are you listening to me, Kunikida?

00:02:13.870 --> 00:02:15.990
Don't mind me, Rampo-san.

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:19.490
It's only right for a 
suspect to be detained.

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:21.950
You're suspected of murder.

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:25.590
The girl set off the 
grenades with her own hands.

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:26.910
That's your claim.

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:32.640
But there are no witnesses, and all 
evidence was destroyed by the enemy.

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:34.930
They even went to the trouble

00:02:34.930 --> 00:02:37.750
of making sure the grenades matched 
the model used by the Agency.

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:40.390
You've been framed.

00:02:40.820 --> 00:02:42.940
Part of an operation by the Rats.

00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:45.570
Or rather, a way to harass us 
that happened to be convenient.

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:47.780
I...

00:02:48.670 --> 00:02:51.140
Will you accept the charge out of guilt?

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:54.480
I don't care about your inner conflict.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:57.360
I'm making sure you're found innocent.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:01.850
The Rats must have someone who 
specializes in destroying evidence.

00:03:01.850 --> 00:03:03.430
We'll capture him.

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:06.150
I won't let anyone object.

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:09.240
Not the Agency or the boss.

00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:10.600
Rampo-san...

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:11.910
Why go to such lengths?

00:03:13.590 --> 00:03:18.190
If I'd seen through demon Fyodor's trap,

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:22.630
<b><i>A Perfect Murder
and Murderer (Part 1)</i></b>

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:22.630
Episode 41

00:03:19.350 --> 00:03:21.290
the girl wouldn't have died.

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:29.560
<b>Yasei Jidai</b>

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:29.560
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:29.560
Challenging.

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:36.380
Anything that torments the grand intellect 
of one such as myself, Poe, is to be feared.

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:41.030
Still, I shall be the first to solve 
this mystery of the far east!

00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:54.400
Poe-kun!

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:55.660
What a coincidence.

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:57.480
R-Rampo-kun?

00:03:57.480 --> 00:03:59.010
Whatcha doing here?

00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:00.950
Oh.

00:04:00.950 --> 00:04:02.000
Waiting for someone?

00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:04.300
He figured me out!

00:04:04.940 --> 00:04:07.390
I won something in an auction.

00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:08.930
I'm here to retrieve it.

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:11.460
And what brings you here, Rampo-kun?

00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:12.820
Also...

00:04:13.180 --> 00:04:15.280
Why are you dressed like that?

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:18.400
Finally, someone notices it.

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:22.630
I went against the boss's orders 
in the cannibalism incident.

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:27.020
He had me work as the mascot 
of the company, so I ran away.

00:04:27.390 --> 00:04:30.140
Anyway, good seeing you here!

00:04:30.140 --> 00:04:31.660
Give me a hand!

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:33.850
R-Rampo-kun!

00:04:33.850 --> 00:04:36.020
I'm supposed to be meeting someone!

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:38.790
Karl bit me!

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:41.660
I see.

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:47.610
So this enemy "evidence destroyer" will 
be showing up at this observation deck.

00:04:47.610 --> 00:04:48.440
<i>Yup.</i>

00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:51.560
<i>Then wouldn't it be better 
if you helped me spot them?</i>

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:53.130
He knows who I am.

00:04:53.530 --> 00:04:57.480
The evidence destroyer is Fyodor's 
ally and right-hand man.

00:04:57.860 --> 00:05:00.050
<i>An expert in information manipulation.</i>

00:05:00.050 --> 00:05:03.060
<i>I have prior arrangements...</i>

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:06.650
<i>But I have a hard time 
saying no to Rampo-kun.</i>

00:05:06.910 --> 00:05:10.660
<i>The only info we have on the evidence 
destroyer is the photo I gave you.</i>

00:05:12.890 --> 00:05:15.690
He looks like he wouldn't have many friends.

00:05:15.690 --> 00:05:17.570
You're not one to talk.

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:19.670
Though...

00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:23.410
What made you suspect he will show up here?

00:05:23.780 --> 00:05:25.810
<i>A Gifted that we captured fessed up.</i>

00:05:26.590 --> 00:05:27.390
<i>Then again...</i>

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:30.880
He seemed like a skeevy little grunt.

00:05:31.190 --> 00:05:32.960
<i>It might have been bogus.</i>

00:05:34.780 --> 00:05:36.680
The time's passed.

00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:38.630
He hasn't shown up.

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:40.680
I'm bored.

00:05:40.680 --> 00:05:42.640
Poe-kun, say something funny.

00:05:42.640 --> 00:05:43.680
That's a tall order!

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:49.910
Oh, how about I tell you about the 
mystery I've been working on?

00:05:50.270 --> 00:05:52.120
The talk of the town is...

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:52.880
No!

00:05:52.880 --> 00:05:54.450
Mystery?!

00:05:54.450 --> 00:05:57.440
I'd rather play with the 
kids in the neighborhood.

00:05:57.440 --> 00:05:58.570
<i>Oh, no.</i>

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:01.880
This author has in fact been murdered.

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:05.810
In the exact same way he 
described in his novel, in fact.

00:06:07.650 --> 00:06:11.340
The first three chapters of the 
novel were published in a magazine.

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:15.350
He died right after the manuscript 
for the fourth and final chapter,

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:17.870
the resolution, was finished.

00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:23.330
And, after the crime, the murderer stole 
the fourth chapter from the scene.

00:06:23.330 --> 00:06:24.720
Why?

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:30.730
Because the truth and trick behind the 
murder was written in the fourth chapter.

00:06:31.020 --> 00:06:34.950
The victim was a mystery novelist
 using the pen name "Kindaichi."

00:06:34.950 --> 00:06:38.570
He was a well-known, talented author, 
so his death set the public astir.

00:06:38.570 --> 00:06:41.170
The entire industry pored over
 the first three chapters,

00:06:41.170 --> 00:06:43.800
but alas, they all failed
 to solve the mystery.

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:47.300
I'm working on it myself, 
but it's quite the—

00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:49.180
Rampo-kun?!

00:06:49.180 --> 00:06:50.880
You don't have anything better to do, huh?

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:53.280
Weren't you supposed to 
wait on another floor?

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:56.560
I'm pissed that he hasn't shown up, 
so I came up with a way to blow off steam.

00:06:56.880 --> 00:06:59.520
I'm going to guess who murdered 
the author right here.

00:07:00.170 --> 00:07:02.230
S-Stop it!

00:07:02.230 --> 00:07:04.060
We'll know who did it by 
tomorrow, either way.

00:07:04.370 --> 00:07:05.430
Tomorrow?

00:07:05.430 --> 00:07:06.250
How?

00:07:06.250 --> 00:07:09.570
The murderer had two motives: 
revenge and money.

00:07:10.050 --> 00:07:13.620
The murderer was told what 
happens in the fourth chapter,

00:07:13.890 --> 00:07:16.620
which means they were pretty 
close to the victim.

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:18.990
That's what triggered his murderous intent.

00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:23.090
So why did he kill him right after 
he finished writing the manuscript?

00:07:23.090 --> 00:07:25.170
Because he'd been waiting for him to.

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:28.380
The more public interest 
there is in the murder,

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:30.590
<i>{<b></b></i>The Killing of Kindaichi

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:30.590
<b>Chapter Four</b>

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:30.590
the more valuable the manuscript becomes.

00:07:30.590 --> 00:07:32.140
And he was planning on selling it.

00:07:32.140 --> 00:07:34.300
He wasn't necessarily 
going to sell it, was he?

00:07:34.590 --> 00:07:35.730
Of course he would.

00:07:35.730 --> 00:07:37.010
In fact, he already has.

00:07:37.010 --> 00:07:37.980
To whom?

00:07:37.980 --> 00:07:38.850
You.

00:07:40.840 --> 00:07:43.360
Your excellent assistant told me.

00:07:43.700 --> 00:07:46.930
It's dangerous and a hassle to bring a small 
animal to a crowded area on a weekend.

00:07:46.930 --> 00:07:50.210
You had to bring him here 
anyway for your rendezvous.

00:07:50.210 --> 00:07:52.730
In other words, you don't know each other.

00:07:52.730 --> 00:07:54.740
Also, you mentioned an auction.

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:58.200
The best place to sell the controversial 
fourth chapter would be an underground auction.

00:07:58.600 --> 00:08:00.090
Want me to continue?

00:08:04.280 --> 00:08:06.780
I wanted to solve the crime myself!

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:11.990
But if the police bought the manuscript,
 the truth would come out in the news.

00:08:11.990 --> 00:08:13.640
It's a proper piece of evidence.

00:08:13.640 --> 00:08:16.270
Give it to the police, and they'll 
give you a letter of appreciation.

00:08:16.270 --> 00:08:17.910
That's what I'll do!

00:08:17.910 --> 00:08:20.680
I only spent 20 million on it, after all.

00:08:22.220 --> 00:08:24.170
Why that face?

00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:27.380
Master Architect is the 
third-highest rank in the Guild.

00:08:27.380 --> 00:08:30.270
I'll have forgotten I paid 
such an amount by tomorrow.

00:08:30.270 --> 00:08:32.070
Are you mental?!

00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:36.130
I got to see your rare exasperated face,
 so it was well worth the money!

00:08:36.130 --> 00:08:39.270
Now, I shall have to finish the transaction.

00:08:39.270 --> 00:08:43.380
I was told it would be given to me by 
someone with a bright red envelope.

00:08:43.380 --> 00:08:46.170
There's a bright red envelope over there.

00:08:47.020 --> 00:08:48.050
When did that get there?

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:09.000
That man's face just now...

00:09:10.350 --> 00:09:11.690
It's the evidence destroyer!

00:09:12.470 --> 00:09:13.750
Well, damn.

00:09:14.270 --> 00:09:17.460
Turns out this is a good mystery.

00:09:21.900 --> 00:09:23.540
Dead on impact.

00:09:23.930 --> 00:09:25.930
Could this be a suicide?

00:09:25.930 --> 00:09:27.950
Or was he silenced by the Rats?

00:09:32.820 --> 00:09:33.690
Municipal Police!

00:09:33.690 --> 00:09:34.890
Don't touch the body!

00:09:35.390 --> 00:09:36.930
Huh? It's you two.

00:09:38.430 --> 00:09:39.600
Rampo-kun?

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:41.280
Minoura-san!

00:09:42.770 --> 00:09:44.960
Let go!

00:09:44.960 --> 00:09:46.420
Get off me!

00:09:45.130 --> 00:09:47.260
You're the best!

00:09:47.260 --> 00:09:48.770
Now I win!

00:09:49.120 --> 00:09:52.250
P-Please help Minoura-san!

00:09:53.050 --> 00:09:56.100
Why did Rampo-kun suddenly 
become so excited?

00:09:56.100 --> 00:09:56.700
Um...

00:09:56.700 --> 00:09:59.450
Because the police arrived so quickly.

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:03.860
The police arrived just as 
we rushed to the ground.

00:10:03.860 --> 00:10:04.660
Why?

00:10:04.970 --> 00:10:07.400
Because the perpetrator called them.

00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:08.640
Ahead of time.

00:10:08.640 --> 00:10:12.860
To have the municipal police close the area, 
so I wouldn't touch the body.

00:10:13.410 --> 00:10:18.350
So it wasn't a suicide, but something 
the Rats did to silence him?

00:10:18.350 --> 00:10:19.840
Neither.

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:21.100
Look at this.

00:10:21.100 --> 00:10:23.510
The victim's shoe.

00:10:23.510 --> 00:10:25.350
It came off as he was falling.

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:28.930
He had it on when we 
saw him through the window.

00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:32.510
You made that observation 
in that split second?

00:10:32.510 --> 00:10:36.560
Judging by how worn the sole is,
 he must have been wearing it for quite a while.

00:10:36.560 --> 00:10:38.120
It wouldn't have come off so easily.

00:10:38.120 --> 00:10:40.320
So why did it come off mid-air?

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:42.550
I see!

00:10:42.550 --> 00:10:43.870
Hey, explain.

00:10:44.350 --> 00:10:48.210
This shoe wasn't one that the victim 
had been wearing for a long time.

00:10:48.210 --> 00:10:50.610
He was forced to put it on 
just prior to being pushed.

00:10:51.260 --> 00:10:55.180
Because Rampo-kun already knows 
what the footprint looks like.

00:10:56.190 --> 00:10:58.530
I went to their hideout 
in the abandoned mines

00:10:58.530 --> 00:11:00.500
to look for leads on the evidence destroyer.

00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:04.460
Needless to say, I took note of all 
of the footprints on the ground.

00:11:04.460 --> 00:11:06.210
What about this shoe?

00:11:06.210 --> 00:11:07.590
I saw it, too, of course.

00:11:07.590 --> 00:11:10.750
So that face was a forgery 
connected to a fishing line?

00:11:10.750 --> 00:11:11.630
Yup.

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:18.980
They smashed the victim's face in 
and put on a mask used in films,

00:11:18.980 --> 00:11:22.000
then they attached the 
fishing line to the mask

00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:25.620
and adjusted its length so it 
would get caught on his way down.

00:11:32.530 --> 00:11:34.480
Once he hit the ground,

00:11:34.480 --> 00:11:37.470
you wouldn't know his face had 
been smashed in ahead of time.

00:11:37.470 --> 00:11:38.830
So...

00:11:38.830 --> 00:11:42.540
The evidence destroyer himself shoved 
the victim down to cover his tracks.

00:11:42.540 --> 00:11:43.680
So...

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:47.390
I just need to use this to determine 
his whereabouts, and it's over.

00:11:48.160 --> 00:11:50.540
<i>What is he, a freak?</i>

00:11:50.540 --> 00:11:56.190
<i>I went to the auction to fund my escape 
and throw the Detective Agency off.</i>

00:11:56.190 --> 00:11:58.450
<i>He blew my elegant scheme with 
the wear on a single shoe!</i>

00:11:58.450 --> 00:12:01.650
<i>Just forging that face was a ton of work.</i>

00:12:02.060 --> 00:12:03.980
<i>This situation...</i>

00:12:06.510 --> 00:12:08.910
<i>is exactly as I planned!</i>

00:12:15.490 --> 00:12:16.590
Behold!

00:12:18.710 --> 00:12:21.670
Even the demon of the north 
feared my special ability.

00:12:21.670 --> 00:12:23.000
Know defeat, detective!

00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:25.210
Your insights are inadequate!

00:12:25.210 --> 00:12:28.370
Special Ability: The Perfect Crime!

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:30.180
<b>The Perfect Crime</b>

00:12:47.690 --> 00:12:49.700
And it's finally time!

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:52.900
Time for the Super Deduction ability 
to instantly reveal the truth of the matter!

00:12:53.430 --> 00:12:55.530
Are you that detective's fan or something?

00:12:55.530 --> 00:12:56.550
I am his rival!

00:13:10.510 --> 00:13:11.800
I don't know...

00:13:13.190 --> 00:13:14.340
What did you just say?

00:13:19.220 --> 00:13:21.220
I can't figure it out at all.

00:13:24.550 --> 00:13:26.290
Silly detectives!

00:13:26.770 --> 00:13:31.150
Wretched hyenas! You'll never catch me.

00:13:31.180 --> 00:13:36.870
<b>
m 0 0 l 73 0 73 240 0 240</b>

00:13:31.500 --> 00:13:36.870
For my special ability is the ability 
to erase the evidence of any crime.

00:13:31.950 --> 00:13:36.870
<b>Special 
Ability: 
The
 Perfect
 Crime</b>

00:13:33.120 --> 00:13:36.870
<b>O
g
u
r
i

00:13:36.870 --> 00:13:41.080
The gates of Heaven are closed, 
never to be opened again.

00:13:41.430 --> 00:13:44.850
I am the ultimate detective killer!

00:13:44.850 --> 00:13:47.470
His coworker's innocence 
will never be proven.

00:13:48.270 --> 00:13:49.520
And...

00:13:50.000 --> 00:13:56.050
He'll never be able to speak of why 
Fyodor let me capture him.

00:14:01.980 --> 00:14:05.610
<b>Two months ago</b>

00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:26.390
Greetings, Mushitaro-san.

00:14:26.650 --> 00:14:28.550
And who are you?

00:14:28.550 --> 00:14:31.300
I'm the man who is going to free you.

00:14:31.740 --> 00:14:34.260
A crime organization locked you up

00:14:34.260 --> 00:14:40.000
to make money off your fantastic ability 
to erase all evidence of a crime.

00:14:41.030 --> 00:14:42.760
Until today.

00:14:43.680 --> 00:14:46.520
The cost for your freedom is rather modest.

00:14:46.520 --> 00:14:50.110
We'd like you to cooperate 
with our operation, just once.

00:14:50.490 --> 00:14:53.870
Between a tyrant and a demon, 
I'd rather make a pact with the demon.

00:14:53.870 --> 00:14:55.780
That's just how I am.

00:14:56.350 --> 00:14:58.410
I'll accept your offer,

00:14:59.850 --> 00:15:02.210
but I have a few conditions.

00:15:02.210 --> 00:15:05.880
First, I will never appear in public.

00:15:06.550 --> 00:15:08.750
I'm only going to use my special ability.

00:15:09.050 --> 00:15:12.310
Second, prepare a desk for my work.

00:15:12.850 --> 00:15:16.530
Even better if you can supply books 
on mysticism and ancient alchemy.

00:15:16.530 --> 00:15:19.750
Third, my meals will be served 
on silver or porcelain dishware.

00:15:20.340 --> 00:15:23.240
Also, my clothes are always to be starched.

00:15:23.240 --> 00:15:24.570
That's fine.

00:15:24.570 --> 00:15:25.600
Anything else?

00:15:26.310 --> 00:15:27.510
Yes.

00:15:27.510 --> 00:15:29.430
This is the most important condition.

00:15:29.820 --> 00:15:35.570
After the operation, I'll need to flee 
overseas to evade the organization,

00:15:35.570 --> 00:15:38.670
but that must happen a 
week after the operation.

00:15:38.670 --> 00:15:40.390
A week after?

00:15:40.390 --> 00:15:42.490
I could have that arranged the day after.

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:45.050
There's something I have left unfinished.

00:15:45.050 --> 00:15:46.960
A promise of death and crime...

00:15:47.590 --> 00:15:52.580
There's a man who, a week after,

00:15:53.530 --> 00:15:54.950
I'd like to kill.

00:16:08.530 --> 00:16:13.490
Rampo-kun hasn't said a single thing 
since he started staring at the body.

00:16:13.490 --> 00:16:14.040
Yeah.

00:16:14.580 --> 00:16:18.280
He'd normally be laughing out loud
 and pointing out the murderer.

00:16:18.280 --> 00:16:22.830
<i>His ability as a detective is 
the very backbone of his soul.</i>

00:16:23.150 --> 00:16:27.640
<i>To have that broken... 
He may never walk again.</i>

00:16:30.740 --> 00:16:33.010
Rampo-kun, don't be so hard on yourself—

00:16:34.060 --> 00:16:35.320
Time to give up!

00:16:36.360 --> 00:16:38.340
Okay, I'm going back to the office.

00:16:38.340 --> 00:16:39.940
You can deal with this mess.

00:16:40.620 --> 00:16:42.150
Rampo-kun...

00:16:44.920 --> 00:16:46.900
<i>My victory is set in stone.</i>

00:16:47.190 --> 00:16:51.910
<i>The photo of me that the Agency has is from 
before I changed my face in the organization,</i>

00:16:51.910 --> 00:16:55.150
<i>which means that they'll never recognize me.</i>

00:16:55.150 --> 00:16:58.820
<i>Killing is as easy for 
me as bending a finger.</i>

00:16:59.610 --> 00:17:03.170
<i>Even when I killed him the other day...</i>

00:17:04.210 --> 00:17:06.540
Mushi-kun, you know...

00:17:06.980 --> 00:17:09.580
I want to write the ultimate mystery.

00:17:22.740 --> 00:17:24.770
Kneel before me, detectives!

00:17:24.770 --> 00:17:26.480
I am the king of crime!

00:17:26.860 --> 00:17:31.370
None can force me to repent 
or admit to my crimes!

00:17:31.370 --> 00:17:32.950
Hey, there. Got a minute?

00:17:34.690 --> 00:17:35.890
<i>The detective!</i>

00:17:35.890 --> 00:17:37.300
<i>Why is he here?</i>

00:17:37.300 --> 00:17:38.570
<i>Is he on to me?</i>

00:17:38.570 --> 00:17:39.650
<i>Impossible.</i>

00:17:39.650 --> 00:17:42.250
Do you know where the taxi stop is?

00:17:42.950 --> 00:17:44.030
Taxi?

00:17:44.030 --> 00:17:48.050
I was going to take the 
taxi back to the office,

00:17:48.050 --> 00:17:50.510
but the main street's been blocked off 
by the police because of the incident.

00:17:50.880 --> 00:17:54.970
I thought I'd find a 
taxi on this back street,

00:17:54.970 --> 00:17:57.170
but you're the only person 
around that I can ask.

00:17:57.500 --> 00:18:00.550
<i>Hasn't he realized who I am?</i>

00:18:01.210 --> 00:18:03.830
<i>It's true, the main road's closed.</i>

00:18:03.830 --> 00:18:06.050
<i>This is the only place to find a taxi.</i>

00:18:06.480 --> 00:18:08.660
<i>What a comical situation.</i>

00:18:08.660 --> 00:18:10.940
<i>The detective, on his way home 
after giving up on a case,</i>

00:18:10.940 --> 00:18:13.770
<i>strikes up a conversation with the perpetrator!</i>

00:18:14.110 --> 00:18:17.300
Sorry, but I can't think of any nearby taxi stops.

00:18:18.270 --> 00:18:19.990
Fine. I'll just wait here, then.

00:18:19.990 --> 00:18:21.890
<i>You're waiting here?!</i>

00:18:21.890 --> 00:18:23.830
<i>I'm meeting my ride here!</i>

00:18:24.090 --> 00:18:27.110
<i>He's going to end up seeing my vehicle!</i>

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:31.910
<i>A perfect crime must not leave 
a single loose thread.</i>

00:18:32.260 --> 00:18:34.810
There's a station five minutes from here.

00:18:34.810 --> 00:18:35.600
I'll draw you a map.

00:18:35.600 --> 00:18:36.080
No!

00:18:36.080 --> 00:18:37.270
I don't wanna walk!

00:18:38.970 --> 00:18:43.850
Okay, let's do this. There's a bus station 
nearby that'll take you to the station.

00:18:43.850 --> 00:18:44.770
Take that, and—

00:18:44.770 --> 00:18:47.260
No buses! No trains! Too much work!

00:18:47.260 --> 00:18:49.880
Also, I don't know how to take trains.

00:18:49.880 --> 00:18:51.640
<i>What are you, a grade school kid?!</i>

00:18:51.950 --> 00:18:53.010
I know!

00:18:53.010 --> 00:18:56.180
I don't want to have to walk, 
so can you give me a piggyback ride?

00:18:56.180 --> 00:18:58.420
That's no request to make 
of another human being!

00:18:58.780 --> 00:19:01.290
I've made the newbie at the 
office do it a few times.

00:19:01.610 --> 00:19:06.320
<i>Have I gotten involved with 
someone I shouldn't have?</i>

00:19:16.110 --> 00:19:18.810
I've arrived, Mushitaro-sama.

00:19:18.810 --> 00:19:21.130
<i>He's already here.</i>

00:19:21.130 --> 00:19:24.160
Sorry, but I have business with this man.

00:19:24.160 --> 00:19:27.530
Pardon me, um...

00:19:27.530 --> 00:19:28.410
Rampo.

00:19:28.410 --> 00:19:31.270
Well, Rampo-kun, I wish you luck.

00:19:38.870 --> 00:19:41.290
<i>He's seen my car.</i>

00:19:41.640 --> 00:19:43.370
<i>Well, whatever.</i>

00:19:43.370 --> 00:19:45.030
<i>It shouldn't be a problem—</i>

00:19:44.000 --> 00:19:46.110
Driver! To the Detective Agency!

00:19:46.440 --> 00:19:47.480
Wh-Wh-Wh...

00:19:47.480 --> 00:19:48.070
You good?

00:19:48.070 --> 00:19:49.440
What are you doing?!

00:19:49.440 --> 00:19:51.490
This vehicle is here for me!

00:19:51.490 --> 00:19:52.930
It's hot, huh?

00:19:52.930 --> 00:19:54.190
Turn on the AC, please.

00:19:54.190 --> 00:19:55.200
Are you listening?

00:19:55.480 --> 00:19:56.740
I have a good idea.

00:19:56.740 --> 00:20:00.030
I'll pay you back if you let me
 take the car with you.

00:20:00.030 --> 00:20:02.930
I could hook you up with work
 if you ever need it, for example.

00:20:03.240 --> 00:20:04.190
<i>No!</i>

00:20:05.060 --> 00:20:06.930
Great. Thanks.

00:20:08.610 --> 00:20:10.110
<i>What do you want me to do?!</i>

00:20:10.110 --> 00:20:11.930
<i>It's not like I want him here, either!</i>

00:20:11.930 --> 00:20:12.690
<i>Alas...</i>

00:20:12.690 --> 00:20:15.020
<i>I can't let this lucky detective 
get any closer to the truth</i>

00:20:15.020 --> 00:20:17.640
<i>than he already has 
just by stumbling across me!</i>

00:20:18.100 --> 00:20:20.330
Please take him to the station.

00:20:20.330 --> 00:20:22.850
Let's have him take a taxi from there.

00:20:22.850 --> 00:20:24.120
Yay!

00:20:27.930 --> 00:20:30.760
Say, what do you do there?

00:20:30.760 --> 00:20:32.400
I'm a detective.

00:20:34.550 --> 00:20:35.790
I see.

00:20:35.790 --> 00:20:38.010
That's a gruesome situation.

00:20:38.010 --> 00:20:40.590
Such a foreign world as 
far as I'm concerned.

00:20:40.990 --> 00:20:43.240
I have just one lead on the murderer.

00:20:43.240 --> 00:20:47.670
He swapped shoes with the victim, so his 
shoes are too small for him right now.

00:20:49.750 --> 00:20:52.830
I know why this case is so hard.

00:20:52.830 --> 00:20:56.230
The murderer is Gifted, with an 
ability of the reality-altering sort.

00:20:56.540 --> 00:20:58.550
<i>He's already figured out that much?!</i>

00:20:58.550 --> 00:21:01.220
My ability as a detective 
boils down to technique.

00:21:01.220 --> 00:21:02.810
Because it isn't a power,

00:21:02.810 --> 00:21:05.270
I don't stand a chance against a 
reality-altering special ability.

00:21:05.880 --> 00:21:07.190
<i>Exactly.</i>

00:21:07.190 --> 00:21:09.960
Although, I managed to 
figure it out this time.

00:21:10.320 --> 00:21:11.290
<i>No!</i>

00:21:11.290 --> 00:21:12.090
<i>Impossible!</i>

00:21:13.210 --> 00:21:14.700
Are you interested?

00:21:14.980 --> 00:21:17.610
That would make for some 
great entertainment.

00:21:17.610 --> 00:21:22.310
To think I'd get to hear how a 
detective I just met solved a crime...

00:21:22.310 --> 00:21:25.330
All right. I'll tell you just this once,
 as thanks for the ride.

00:21:25.750 --> 00:21:28.280
The bright red envelope is the key.

00:21:28.280 --> 00:21:31.840
The evidence destroyer wanted 
me to believe he was dead.

00:21:31.840 --> 00:21:35.640
That's when he took notice 
of my friend, Poe-kun.

00:21:35.640 --> 00:21:38.160
Poe arranged to buy the manuscript and,

00:21:38.660 --> 00:21:43.810
the instant we took it, the evidence 
destroyer pushed a double off the building.

00:21:44.530 --> 00:21:47.620
All for the purpose of 
showcasing that one moment.

00:21:49.130 --> 00:21:55.410
So, where did the perpetrator get 
the envelope and the manuscript?

00:21:56.030 --> 00:21:57.870
The answer's simple.

00:21:58.430 --> 00:22:00.430
He killed and stole it...

00:22:01.330 --> 00:22:03.460
From the author himself.

00:23:37.730 --> 00:23:40.010
<i>A Perfect Murder
 and Murderer (Part 2)</i>

00:23:37.730 --> 00:23:40.010
Next Episode: 42
